#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# inverse_jacobi_nd

#% text
# `inverse_jacobi_nd(v, m)` gives the `u` with `jacobi_nd(u, m) = v`, the inverse of the Jacobi elliptic function `nd`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is the principal branch of DLMF 22.15, real for a real `v` in the range of the function on the real line and `0 <= m < 1`.
#% item
# For a real `m > 1` the value is `inverse_jacobi_nc(v, 1/m)/sqrt(m)` (the reciprocal-modulus transformation, DLMF 22.17), real for a real `v` in the range of the function on the real line.

#% item
# Machine numbers and balls give numerical values; exact arguments stay unevaluated.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_nd(1.2, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.9578977976026843

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_nd(1.0, 0.5)
#% output
#= 0.0

#% cell
inverse_jacobi_nd(1.1, 0.3)
#% output
#= 0.8945735832606405

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `jacobi_nd` undoes it:

#% cell
jacobi_nd(inverse_jacobi_nd(1.2, 0.4), 0.4)
#% output
#= 1.2

#% text
# The inverse grows to the quarter period `K(m)` at the end of the range:

#% cell
[inverse_jacobi_nd(sqrt(2.0), 0.5), elliptic_k(0.5)]
#% output
#= [1.854074677301372, 1.8540746773013719]

